1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,508
[phone ringing]

2
00:00:07,633 --> 00:00:09,176
She's not at the truck!

3
00:00:10,219 --> 00:00:11,637
I haven't seen her
around here either.

4
00:00:11,762 --> 00:00:13,805
[ringing continues]

5
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,477
[sighs]

6
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:21,647
Is she not answering the phone?

7
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:23,231
No.

8
00:00:23,232 --> 00:00:24,732
She hasn't texted back either?

9
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:27,194
I've been texting her.
She hasn't read or replied.

10
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:29,237
- Nothing?
- No.

11
00:00:29,238 --> 00:00:31,281
[suspenseful music playing]

12
00:00:32,324 --> 00:00:33,408
What now?

13
00:00:36,662 --> 00:00:38,330
[Feng] Boss?

14
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:39,665
Boss?

15
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,585
We'll be late
if we don't set off now.

16
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:50,341
Maybe I'll go on instead?

17
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:51,843
Can you talk to them?

18
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:54,680
Are you kidding? They said
it has to be mixed-gender.

19
00:00:58,225 --> 00:01:00,393
I'm sure she'll show up.

20
00:01:00,394 --> 00:01:01,728
She cares
about Jin Lai Hao the most.

21
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,689
[pants]

22
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:06,400
Wait.

23
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:08,652
What about her grandma?

24
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:12,864
I'll go look for her
at the nursing home.
You guys get going.

25
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:26,711
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

26
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:31,382
[singing in Mandarin]

27
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:33,552
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

28
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:35,761
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

29
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:37,848
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

30
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:40,224
[singing in Mandarin]

31
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:44,270
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

32
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:47,149
[singing in Mandarin]

33
00:01:53,864 --> 00:01:56,824
[nurse] Recently, Yu-chih's
blood pressure sometimes drops
rather low late at night,

34
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:59,243
but it seems
to have gotten better
these last couple of days.

35
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,829
Maybe it's because his favorite
big sister is going to compete
in the finals.

36
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,414
[nurse] Yeah, maybe.

37
00:02:03,415 --> 00:02:05,499
They still respond to things
around them sometimes.

38
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,835
We'll observe
for a couple of days.

39
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:09,254
Let us know
if anything comes up.

40
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:11,297
- Okay. Thanks.
- [nurse] Yeah.

41
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:13,342
[machine beeping]

42
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:17,596
[footsteps approaching]

43
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:25,812
- Has Ma Yu-li been here?
- No.

44
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:28,774
You're competing
in the finals today, right?

45
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:31,442
Yes, we are,
but we can't find her anywhere.

46
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:33,654
She's not answering calls
or replying to our texts.

47
00:02:33,779 --> 00:02:35,781
Calm down.

48
00:02:35,906 --> 00:02:39,283
She wouldn't get
cold feet and run away
without telling you guys.

49
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:40,827
[line ringing]

50
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:43,455
- [operator]
<i>Your call will be...</i>
- Yeah, I know.

51
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:48,335
Where else could she be?

52
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:51,254
We've looked everywhere.
And I'm here now.

53
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,175
What about her hometown?

54
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:58,804
That's impossible.
She doesn't get along
with her dad.

55
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:02,724
[dramatic music playing]

56
00:03:12,234 --> 00:03:14,695
[operator] <i>Your call
will be redirected to...</i>

57
00:03:16,238 --> 00:03:17,489
[sighs]

58
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:24,287
Who are you to Yu-li?

59
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:29,000
We're just friends.

60
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:31,253
She's not my type.

61
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,756
What the hell?

62
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,676
[sighs]

63
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:41,554
You don't want anybody

64
00:03:41,555 --> 00:03:43,348
getting close
to the girl you like.

65
00:03:43,849 --> 00:03:44,850
I get it.

66
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:50,397
Who said I like her?

67
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:52,690
It's all the same.

68
00:03:52,691 --> 00:03:54,693
You know if you do.

69
00:03:56,528 --> 00:03:59,197
You need to express
your feelings.

70
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:00,741
You might lose everything

71
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:03,785
before you know it.

72
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:27,559
[Mr. Ma] Time to eat.

73
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:32,730
[sighs]

74
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:34,399
No place like home, right?

75
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:36,943
Eat it while it's hot.

76
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,406
Don't be like that.

77
00:04:42,491 --> 00:04:45,743
Look. How do people
think of you now?

78
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:48,413
Do you still have the nerve
to take part in the competition?

79
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:53,834
I won't harm you.

80
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:56,588
I'm the one
who cares about you the most.

81
00:04:57,923 --> 00:05:01,301
You don't care about me.
All you care about is yourself.

82
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:03,553
Of course, I care about you.

83
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:06,765
You're Ma Chih-chieh, my son.

84
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:09,600
Can you give me a break?

85
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:11,602
[emotional music playing]

86
00:05:11,603 --> 00:05:13,355
I'm just being myself.
I've done nothing wrong.

87
00:05:14,356 --> 00:05:17,943
Is that so? Then why
are people trashing you? Huh?

88
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:20,904
I don't care how they trash me.

89
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:24,366
But I want you to support me.

90
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:28,537
Want me to support you
being a sissy?

91
00:05:39,798 --> 00:05:41,049
You're not going anywhere.

92
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:44,970
Just stay here at home
to calm down.

93
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:47,138
Don't go back to that restaurant
to put yourself out there

94
00:05:47,389 --> 00:05:48,889
for people to point fingers
at you.

95
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:51,058
And I want you
to get your hair cut.

96
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:55,521
You'll work for your uncle.
They're all family.

97
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:57,566
Nobody is going to say
anything against you.

98
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:07,993
Remember, you're Ma Chih-chieh.

99
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:10,787
[intense breathing]

100
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:12,747
[door slams]

101
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:20,422
[sniffles]

102
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:25,010
I'm Ma Yu-li!

103
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:32,725
- 30 minutes late?
- Yes.

104
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:34,436
How do we start the competition?

105
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:38,064
Besides, it's a live show.
We can't wait.

106
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,859
[Feng] Here's the deal, sir.

107
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:43,028
We've run into a bit
of a situation with one
of our team members.

108
00:06:43,153 --> 00:06:45,697
We'd like to ask
if you could bend the rules

109
00:06:47,032 --> 00:06:50,784
and allow me
to team up with my boss instead.

110
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,078
[laughs]

111
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:54,873
Even if I say yes, I'm not sure
my superiors will agree.

112
00:06:54,998 --> 00:06:57,833
You know it's hard to predict
public opinion nowadays.

113
00:06:57,834 --> 00:06:59,878
We can't change the rules
at the last minute.

114
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:02,046
If you can't make
a mixed-gender team,

115
00:07:02,047 --> 00:07:04,841
I'll announce
Chang Xin wins, okay?

116
00:07:06,051 --> 00:07:08,595
Wait. You have
this famous influencer.

117
00:07:09,888 --> 00:07:12,765
Put her in
and you'll form your team,

118
00:07:12,766 --> 00:07:14,184
- right?
- [organizer] Well...

119
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:15,894
- How's that?
- [organizer] Good idea.

120
00:07:16,019 --> 00:07:17,228
She's very popular.

121
00:07:17,479 --> 00:07:19,064
- [organizer] It's up to them.
- You're right.

122
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:21,106
I am popular. But what's that
got to do with you?

123
00:07:21,107 --> 00:07:23,692
- Are you the organizer?
- Yes, I am.

124
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:26,905
If you don't do it,
your team will have to withdraw.

125
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:29,157
[tense music playing]

126
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:32,743
It's almost time.

127
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:34,037
- Hurry up.
- Okay.

128
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:41,919
Her popularity will be a bonus.

129
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,213
Maybe you'll go on first.
When Yu-li is here,
she'll take over.

130
00:07:44,214 --> 00:07:47,133
Otherwise, when it's time,
I'll have to announce you've
withdrawn from the competition.

131
00:07:47,258 --> 00:07:50,178
Just because I'm a foodie
doesn't mean I can cook.

132
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,932
Fine. Give us a minute.
Yi-hsuan?

133
00:07:54,057 --> 00:07:56,558
I think you'll really have
to step up and replace her.

134
00:07:56,559 --> 00:07:59,813
If you don't, we won't even
be qualified. It's embarrassing
to lose because of that.

135
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:01,272
Don't worry.

136
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:04,109
We're making Red Sea Crab
with Glutinous Rice.
It was my dad's best dish.

137
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:07,696
And I've brought
a secret weapon.
I'm sure you can do it.

138
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:22,252
Her boots are here.

139
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,049
[Mr. Ma] Who is it?

140
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,135
[Wen] Delivery.

141
00:08:36,141 --> 00:08:37,975
Is Ma Yu-li here?

142
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:39,893
No, he's not.

143
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:41,813
What are you doing?
It's my home!

144
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:45,024
Mr. Ma, don't stop him.

145
00:08:45,025 --> 00:08:46,650
They need to go
to the competition.

146
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:48,028
[Chin-nan] Ma Yu-li!

147
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:49,863
Yu-li?

148
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:51,990
[upbeat music playing]

149
00:08:52,574 --> 00:08:53,825
[Yu-li] I'm here!

150
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:58,037
- Here!
- [Chin-nan] Wait!
I'll open the door!

151
00:08:58,038 --> 00:08:59,998
What you're doing
will screw him up. Move!

152
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:02,834
[screams, winces]

153
00:09:06,838 --> 00:09:08,339
Let go!

154
00:09:08,590 --> 00:09:12,177
I have a son like yours.
I know how you feel.

155
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,695
Are you okay?

156
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:32,989
They're all waiting for you.

157
00:09:34,616 --> 00:09:35,700
Mm-hmm.

158
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:38,244
[Mr. Ma] Let go!

159
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:41,706
Wen? He's my dad. Don't. Wen.

160
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:44,292
Dad.

161
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:48,630
Dad,

162
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:51,758
I know what I'm doing.

163
00:09:53,218 --> 00:09:54,719
And I know I can do a great job.

164
00:09:58,348 --> 00:10:00,266
- Go now.
- [Chin-nan] Let's go.

165
00:10:00,391 --> 00:10:02,602
[music continues]

166
00:10:16,908 --> 00:10:18,909
[singer] <i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

167
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:20,954
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

168
00:10:21,079 --> 00:10:23,248
Will your dad be okay?

169
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:29,003
[singer]
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

170
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,757
- Hey...
- Huh?

171
00:10:36,094 --> 00:10:39,264
From now on,
I won't let you go.

172
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:41,850
Huh?

173
00:10:43,101 --> 00:10:45,270
I'm confessing
my feelings for you.

174
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:55,947
What are you talking about?

175
00:10:58,324 --> 00:11:00,701
[engine revving]

176
00:11:00,702 --> 00:11:01,828
Hey!

177
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:05,080
Slow down! What are you doing?

178
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:06,291
Lin Chin-nan!

179
00:11:11,296 --> 00:11:13,464
[horn honks]

180
00:11:13,715 --> 00:11:15,133
[Yu-li] Too fast.

181
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:17,801
[dramatic music playing]

182
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:20,305
TAIWANESE CUISINE SHOWDOWN
THE BATTLE OF REBORN CLASSICS

183
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:25,142
FINALS

184
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:27,854
[narrator laughs] <i>Okay, guys.</i>
[clears throat]

185
00:11:27,979 --> 00:11:31,316
<i>Tonight is the epic finale
of</i> Super Chef.

186
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:34,819
<i>We have a full house here,
packed with hyped-up
audience,</i>

187
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:39,199
<i>and everyone is screaming
as we crown the king
of Taiwanese cuisine,</i>

188
00:11:39,324 --> 00:11:42,285
<i>who will win the prize
of one million dollars.</i>

189
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:45,163
<i>After two months
of brutal battles,</i>

190
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:47,789
<i>Chang Xin and Jin Lai Hao
have fought their way
to the finals.</i>

191
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:50,835
<i>They'll fight to the very end
with their signature dishes
tonight.</i>

192
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:54,214
<i>What?
Is this a twist of fate?</i>

193
00:11:54,339 --> 00:11:58,134
<i>They've both chosen to finish
with glutinous rice.</i>

194
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,054
<i>Chang Xin is going
with a delicate style.</i>

195
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:03,514
<i>They're using lobsters
and abalone</i>

196
00:12:03,765 --> 00:12:07,227
<i>to take the dish up a notch
to a state-banquet level
luxurious delicacy.</i>

197
00:12:07,352 --> 00:12:09,436
CHANG XIN

198
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:12,105
JIN LAI HAO

199
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:15,318
<i>Meanwhile, Jin Lai Hao
faces the challenge
with a family secret weapon.</i>

200
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:19,112
<i>But they're in trouble.</i>

201
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:23,075
<i>Yu-li from Jin Lai Hao
mysteriously lost contact
at this critical moment.</i>

202
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:27,037
<i>Famous influencer Queen
of Reviews has stepped in
to replace her.</i>

203
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:30,207
<i>Can she give Jin Lai Hao
a chance of winning?</i>

204
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:32,210
<i>Can Jin Lai Hao
turn the tables,</i>

205
00:12:32,335 --> 00:12:34,545
<i>or will Chang Xin
walk away with the victory?</i>

206
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:36,923
<i>Let's stay tuned to find out.</i>

207
00:12:45,348 --> 00:12:46,891
I'll show you.

208
00:12:50,812 --> 00:12:53,564
Use a roll cut. Cut and roll it.

209
00:12:55,066 --> 00:12:57,317
Cut and roll it. Hmm?

210
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:59,111
- Okay. Roll it.
- Try it.

211
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:01,364
- You can do it.
- Cooking is so hard.

212
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:03,533
[sizzling]

213
00:13:10,123 --> 00:13:11,540
Yi-hsuan, give me
that empty bowl.

214
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:13,376
- What?
- The empty bowl
in front of you.

215
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:20,465
[narrator]
<i>They're in big trouble.</i>

216
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:22,342
<i>Jin Lai Hao spilled
their secret weapon.</i>

217
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:24,469
<i>It's said to be
the boss's dad's
special seasoning.</i>

218
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:26,264
<i>But they spilled it.</i>

219
00:13:26,389 --> 00:13:28,266
<i>- It seems like
Chang Xin is destined to win.</i>
- [Yi-hsuan] Sorry.

220
00:13:28,391 --> 00:13:29,433
[groans]

221
00:13:29,434 --> 00:13:31,435
[Yi-hsuan] What now?

222
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:35,188
Give me the shrimp oil.
This is my secret weapon,

223
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:38,275
the special recipe
from our hometown.

224
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:39,319
[Lu-yung] Smells great.

225
00:13:39,444 --> 00:13:41,487
[dramatic music playing]

226
00:13:44,282 --> 00:13:45,366
I'm sorry.

227
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:48,036
I'll wipe it clean.

228
00:13:51,122 --> 00:13:52,457
[groans]

229
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:54,500
She's clumsy.

230
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:58,629
[indistinct chatter]

231
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:04,344
[Yi-hsuan] What do we do now?

232
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:12,518
[upbeat music playing]

233
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:14,187
[Chin-nan]
Excuse us. Coming through.
Sorry, we're in a hurry.

234
00:14:14,312 --> 00:14:15,520
- Excuse us.
- Yu-li!

235
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:17,564
- It's Yu-li!
- Yu-li is here!

236
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:19,983
Fire goddess Ma Yu-li.

237
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:23,196
[narrator] <i>What a turn!
So dramatic!</i>

238
00:14:23,321 --> 00:14:27,867
<i>The Favorite Female Chef,
Ma Yu-li, is back
in the nick of time.</i>

239
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:29,369
[man] Fire goddess Ma Yu-li.

240
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:31,578
You're a professional.

241
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:36,918
[crowd] Fire goddess Ma Yu-li...
Fire goddess Ma Yu-li...

242
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:43,006
You're really here.
We thought you weren't coming.

243
00:14:43,007 --> 00:14:45,051
I've worked hard for so long.
How could I not come?

244
00:14:53,184 --> 00:14:55,268
Glad we made it.

245
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:57,939
You scared me to death.
I have a bad heart.
Don't do this again.

246
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:01,275
- Welcome back.
- How is it going?

247
00:15:03,361 --> 00:15:04,903
The shrimp oil got knocked over.

248
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,072
Huh?

249
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:09,033
I'm trying...

250
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,411
to figure out
if there's any other way.

251
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,208
Sorry, I've messed it up.

252
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:20,086
It's alright.

253
00:15:21,379 --> 00:15:23,339
[music continues]

254
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:46,319
No big deal. I've made
stir-fried sticky rice.

255
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:50,616
Without the right heat
or enough speed,
it'll never taste good.

256
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:54,578
Get those shallots out for me.

257
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:56,914
Boil some water,
blanch the dried shrimp
to get rid of the fishy smell.

258
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,416
Add some carrots
and unused crab legs.

259
00:15:58,541 --> 00:16:00,585
Get the broth ready first.

260
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:03,044
You want the glutinous rice
to absorb the seafood essence
to replace the shrimp oil.

261
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:05,255
Stir-frying for wok hei,
the glutinous rice
will be more aromatic.

262
00:16:05,256 --> 00:16:07,091
- Let's do this.
- Okay.

263
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:12,221
[host] Jin Lai Hao is springing
into action. Seems like
they've found a way out.

264
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:13,431
Go for it.

265
00:16:16,434 --> 00:16:19,770
Dad? How do you think we should
define the restaurant?

266
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:24,484
[Chin-lai]
Make our favorite dishes
with the best ingredients.

267
00:16:26,611 --> 00:16:28,279
This is our signature dish.

268
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:43,544
[Yi-hsuan]
Without the shrimp oil,
will it really work?

269
00:16:44,754 --> 00:16:47,088
It's alright.
There's a way to fix it.

270
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:49,717
As long as she follows
what I taught her,
it'll be alright.

271
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:53,136
With the shrimp oil,
of course it gets done
quickly and beautifully.

272
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:55,430
But now
they're using broth instead

273
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:58,475
to slowly stir-fry the seafood
flavor into the rice.

274
00:16:58,476 --> 00:17:00,644
Stir-fry
while adding it bit by bit.

275
00:17:00,645 --> 00:17:02,146
Don't rush it.

276
00:17:03,314 --> 00:17:07,317
We're playing it safe,
slow and steady.

277
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:08,528
Cool.

278
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:29,674
JUDGES' COMMENTS

279
00:17:29,799 --> 00:17:31,384
[narrator] <i>When both dishes
hit the table...</i>

280
00:17:31,509 --> 00:17:33,635
<i>Oh, my! It's too beautiful,
I can't even look.</i>

281
00:17:33,636 --> 00:17:35,762
<i>Chang Xin's Seafood
with Glutinous Rice</i>

282
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:37,764
<i>has a whole lobster
lying grandly in the center.</i>

283
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:41,560
<i>That bright crimson color
is like my blushing cheeks.</i>

284
00:17:41,561 --> 00:17:44,021
<i>Its aroma wafts over
like sea waves crashing in.</i>

285
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:46,607
<i>It's luxurious and imposing.
Amazing!</i>

286
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:49,401
<i>Next up, Jin Lai Hao's
Red Sea Crab
with Glutinous Rice.</i>

287
00:17:49,402 --> 00:17:51,444
<i>The red sea crab is on top
of the soft glutinous rice.</i>

288
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:55,407
<i>The rich crab flavor
is fully infused
into the rice.</i>

289
00:17:55,408 --> 00:17:57,409
<i>When I watched them
stir-fry it,</i>

290
00:17:57,410 --> 00:18:00,453
<i>I knew its taste
would definitely be
a thumbs-up.</i>

291
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,748
<i>Can we be so blessed?</i>

292
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:07,252
<i>It looks like
the judges have probably
made a decision.</i>

293
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:10,548
<i>But this is so exciting
to watch. It'll be okay.</i>

294
00:18:10,673 --> 00:18:11,716
[host] Thank you.

295
00:18:13,384 --> 00:18:14,801
Throughout this series
of competitions,

296
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:17,597
I believe all contestants
have worked hard,

297
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:20,099
especially the four of them
on this stage.

298
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:22,642
It really hasn't been easy
for them.

299
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:26,689
Now, the highly anticipated
results are finally in.

300
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:29,482
For <i>Super Chef</i> ,

301
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:34,614
with the scores from our
three judges and the votes
from our online audience,

302
00:18:34,739 --> 00:18:38,491
the final winning team is...

303
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:40,620
[dramatic music playing]

304
00:18:46,626 --> 00:18:49,336
Congratulations, Jin Lai Hao.

305
00:18:49,337 --> 00:18:51,631
Ma Yu-li and Chou Lu-yung.

306
00:18:51,756 --> 00:18:52,798
Damn it!

307
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:54,925
[cheers and yells]

308
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,678
<i>Congratulations!</i>

309
00:18:58,679 --> 00:18:59,889
Yes!

310
00:19:00,848 --> 00:19:02,807
Yu-li won! She did it!

311
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:05,603
Yu-li is the winner, Granny!
They're the winners!

312
00:19:05,728 --> 00:19:07,605
- Nice!
- You're the best.

313
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:11,567
Damn!

314
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:16,322
Keep fighting, Yu-chih.

315
00:19:16,447 --> 00:19:18,949
Yu-li has done it.
I know you can too.

316
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:21,202
[yelling]

317
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:26,873
[Chin-nan]
Jin Lai Hao, number one!

318
00:19:26,874 --> 00:19:28,501
We're the winners!

319
00:19:28,626 --> 00:19:31,837
Jin Lai Hao, number one!

320
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:33,422
You've got this.

321
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,175
Cool!

322
00:19:40,763 --> 00:19:42,765
[cheering]

323
00:19:46,644 --> 00:19:49,689
Excuse me, guys.
I have something to say.

324
00:19:51,232 --> 00:19:53,150
[music continues]

325
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,652
<i>I've made up my mind</i>

326
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:58,530
<i>to give up the Favorite
Female Chef award.</i>

327
00:19:58,531 --> 00:19:59,864
JIN LAI HAO, YU-LI, GO FOR IT

328
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,866
YU-LI, GODDESS, I LOVE YOU

329
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:03,411
<i>I'm transgender.</i>

330
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:09,792
I believe
most of you know that.

331
00:20:15,798 --> 00:20:17,842
Whether I win the Favorite
Female Chef or not,

332
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:19,510
I don't care anymore.

333
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:22,847
<i>Even if you all see me
as a boy, it's alright.</i>

334
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:26,225
I just want to be myself,

335
00:20:27,393 --> 00:20:29,228
be a great cook

336
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:31,814
and make delicious food.

337
00:20:33,858 --> 00:20:35,818
I don't cook for any awards.

338
00:20:37,695 --> 00:20:41,198
Please remember me.
I'm Ma Yu-li.

339
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:42,908
[music swells]

340
00:20:47,538 --> 00:20:48,873
Cool!

341
00:20:48,998 --> 00:20:50,708
[cheering]

342
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:57,047
[crowd] Fire Goddess Ma Yu-li...
Fire Goddess Ma Yu-li...

343
00:20:57,298 --> 00:21:00,301
[pensive music playing]

344
00:21:14,732 --> 00:21:16,734
[chuckling]

345
00:21:17,818 --> 00:21:20,571
[device beeping rapidly]

346
00:21:23,741 --> 00:21:25,701
Yu-chih? Yu-chih?

347
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:28,078
[device flatlining]

348
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:31,832
Nurse! Nurse!

349
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:39,465
Congratulations to the winner,
Jin Lai Hao!

350
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:41,050
[cheering]

351
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,468
Our boss is the best.

352
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:44,470
Cheers!

353
00:21:44,595 --> 00:21:46,679
Jin Lai Hao is number one!

354
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,098
Manager!

355
00:21:48,349 --> 00:21:50,434
Boss, she's emptied the bottle.

356
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:52,811
- I'm gonna throw up.
- I'll drink this up.

357
00:21:52,812 --> 00:21:54,980
- [Yu-li] Drink it.
- Let me do it.

358
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:59,442
- Whoa!
- [laughs]

359
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:01,361
[Chin-nan]
Trying to play the hero?

360
00:22:01,362 --> 00:22:02,487
So full!

361
00:22:02,488 --> 00:22:04,657
Where is my hero?

362
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:08,494
Right here!

363
00:22:09,912 --> 00:22:11,663
[Feng] That's right.

364
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:13,123
- [Yi-hsuan] Drink some more.
- You look cool!

365
00:22:13,374 --> 00:22:15,626
- [Yi-hsuan] Drink some more.
- [Yu-li] No.

366
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:22,006
A real hero shows up
when you need him the most.

367
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,133
Right?

368
00:22:25,636 --> 00:22:27,011
- Are they...
- That's...

369
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:28,847
They're dating?

370
00:22:28,848 --> 00:22:31,308
- Yeah.
- Since when?

371
00:22:31,433 --> 00:22:33,519
I knew they'd be together
from the beginning.

372
00:22:33,644 --> 00:22:35,312
Don't be
a Monday morning quarterback.

373
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:37,647
But I mean it.
Am I right or am I right?

374
00:22:37,648 --> 00:22:40,359
Wait. I think it deserves
a drink. Here.

375
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:41,485
[Yu-li] No!

376
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:43,654
My song. My song.

377
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:45,114
Me?

378
00:22:45,364 --> 00:22:46,656
But I can't dance!

379
00:22:46,657 --> 00:22:47,992
Yes, you can.

380
00:22:48,117 --> 00:22:49,994
My legs are like jelly. Wait!

381
00:22:50,119 --> 00:22:52,663
[upbeat music playing]

382
00:22:52,788 --> 00:22:54,665
What are you doing?

383
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:58,001
How do I keep up with you?
Change the move.

384
00:22:58,002 --> 00:22:59,128
[Feng] Forget it.

385
00:22:59,378 --> 00:23:02,381
[singer singing
in foreign language]

386
00:23:15,728 --> 00:23:16,854
Let's dance too.

387
00:24:12,076 --> 00:24:15,079
[soft jazz music playing]

388
00:24:30,552 --> 00:24:32,095
Hey, bro.

389
00:24:32,096 --> 00:24:34,014
It's just a game.

390
00:24:35,933 --> 00:24:37,893
It's not about winning
or losing,

391
00:24:39,103 --> 00:24:41,063
but my dad's expectations of me.

392
00:24:42,272 --> 00:24:43,816
Fine.

393
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:45,942
Don't be so upset.

394
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:48,445
I'll get us two new girls.

395
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:50,447
You'll be fine.

396
00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:51,949
Not in the mood.

397
00:24:52,074 --> 00:24:54,034
Whoa. Whoa!

398
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:57,162
It's really serious. Tim?
The usual.

399
00:24:58,664 --> 00:25:02,584
Listen. You're overthinking it.
Your dad is so with you.

400
00:25:10,801 --> 00:25:12,511
- Forget it.
- What?

401
00:25:12,636 --> 00:25:13,804
You don't know my stress.

402
00:25:14,930 --> 00:25:16,306
I'll never know
if you don't tell me.

403
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:19,810
You should blow off steam
once in a while.

404
00:25:24,148 --> 00:25:26,150
Here. Drink it up.

405
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:29,819
I'll share your burden.

406
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:32,697
Listen. All problems
can be solved by a shot.

407
00:25:32,698 --> 00:25:34,158
- Huh?
- Mm.

408
00:25:37,703 --> 00:25:38,829
Another one.

409
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:41,956
Two for you and one for me.

410
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:43,834
- [Chien-yuan] Damn! Why?
- [man] You've got more problems.

411
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:46,962
[birds chirping]

412
00:25:55,679 --> 00:25:56,805
Hi, Wen.

413
00:26:00,059 --> 00:26:02,227
Brought so much stuff
for your granny?

414
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:04,688
It's for you.

415
00:26:05,189 --> 00:26:07,316
To thank you
for helping me big time.

416
00:26:17,618 --> 00:26:18,744
Where's Yu-chih?

417
00:26:22,039 --> 00:26:23,207
Yu-chih is gone.

418
00:26:24,875 --> 00:26:27,878
[soft music playing]

419
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:29,713
Oh.

420
00:26:34,885 --> 00:26:37,221
[sighs] I wanted to keep it
as a souvenir.

421
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:41,057
But then I thought
that would be stealing.

422
00:26:41,058 --> 00:26:43,310
I think I should give it back
to its owner.

423
00:26:44,728 --> 00:26:46,063
[crying]

424
00:27:02,246 --> 00:27:04,039
Are you alright, Wen?

425
00:27:05,958 --> 00:27:07,084
I'm fine.

426
00:27:08,627 --> 00:27:10,254
I didn't want him to go.

427
00:27:10,379 --> 00:27:12,089
But I'm happy.

428
00:27:13,090 --> 00:27:14,258
Free at last.

429
00:27:16,927 --> 00:27:18,095
I'm free.

430
00:27:18,929 --> 00:27:20,305
Yu-chih is free.

431
00:27:21,265 --> 00:27:23,684
Good. Great.

432
00:27:24,810 --> 00:27:27,813
[dramatic music playing]

433
00:27:34,236 --> 00:27:37,239
[birds chirping]

434
00:27:46,248 --> 00:27:48,000
[Yu-li] Wen!

435
00:27:52,421 --> 00:27:54,131
Hi, old man.

436
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,427
Hi. Why are you here?

437
00:27:59,136 --> 00:28:01,345
We miss you.

438
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:03,724
- [Chin-nan] Miss who?
- [shushes]

439
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,684
[soft music playing]

440
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:07,477
- Come inside.
- [Yu-li] Miss you so much!

441
00:28:07,728 --> 00:28:10,147
So, we asked Yi-hsuan
where you live
and came uninvited.

442
00:28:10,272 --> 00:28:12,649
Fine. Take a seat. Come on.

443
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:16,152
Wen, thank you so much
for helping Jin Lai Hao.

444
00:28:16,153 --> 00:28:18,697
Don't mention it at all.
Take a seat.
Make yourselves at home.

445
00:28:18,822 --> 00:28:20,157
Here.

446
00:28:20,282 --> 00:28:22,033
Can I use your bathroom?

447
00:28:22,034 --> 00:28:23,159
Over there.

448
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:24,286
Hello.

449
00:28:28,123 --> 00:28:31,460
Wen, we've brought
our new dishes
to see what you think.

450
00:28:31,710 --> 00:28:33,836
A taste-test?
I'm not good for that.

451
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:35,338
[Chin-nan] Just taste them.

452
00:28:35,339 --> 00:28:39,926
Our dishes from Jin Lai Hao
are all number one anyway.

453
00:28:39,927 --> 00:28:44,847
- Be humble.
I've got our winning dish here.
- [Wen] Oh!

454
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:47,726
- [Chin-nan] Are you humble?
- [Yu-li] Yeah.

455
00:28:47,851 --> 00:28:49,853
[Wen] Take them all out.
Open them.

456
00:28:54,942 --> 00:28:56,026
Yi-hsuan?

457
00:28:59,029 --> 00:29:01,073
How has your mom been?

458
00:29:02,991 --> 00:29:04,409
She's fine.

459
00:29:04,534 --> 00:29:07,120
She loves to find things to do
to keep herself busy.

460
00:29:10,207 --> 00:29:13,877
I think she misses you
but doesn't want to bother you.

461
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:18,173
And you? Why don't you
ask her out on a date?

462
00:29:25,180 --> 00:29:27,766
I'm old and ugly.
Don't get your mom in trouble.

463
00:29:29,101 --> 00:29:32,020
Is the ego of men like you
made of glass?

464
00:29:45,367 --> 00:29:47,994
Although you're old
and don't look good,

465
00:29:47,995 --> 00:29:52,207
having a dad in a leather jacket
is still pretty cool.

466
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,045
Huh?

467
00:29:57,963 --> 00:30:01,800
To be honest, when I saw you
in this leather jacket as a kid,

468
00:30:01,925 --> 00:30:03,927
I envied your son.

469
00:30:09,057 --> 00:30:10,309
[door opens]

470
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:13,186
[door closes]

471
00:30:16,106 --> 00:30:17,190
[Wen] You've had a long day.

472
00:30:18,942 --> 00:30:20,110
Some midnight snacks?

473
00:30:28,452 --> 00:30:30,954
Yu-chih has gone
to a better place.

474
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:33,123
Here.

475
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:01,651
Things weren't easy
for Yi-hsuan growing up.

476
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:05,197
Glad she has you.

477
00:31:06,323 --> 00:31:07,991
And she's a brave girl.

478
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:12,996
Yeah.

479
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:16,083
We don't need men after all.

480
00:31:19,503 --> 00:31:22,506
[soft music playing]

481
00:31:26,009 --> 00:31:29,096
But a father
can't be replaced by anybody.

482
00:31:34,351 --> 00:31:37,354
Does she want to know
who her real parents are?

483
00:31:43,527 --> 00:31:45,529
She told me once

484
00:31:45,654 --> 00:31:47,697
she wanted to meet
her real parents.

485
00:31:49,199 --> 00:31:51,076
But just that one time.

486
00:31:54,079 --> 00:31:56,164
Maybe she doesn't want
to upset me.

487
00:32:05,715 --> 00:32:07,008
What's wrong?

488
00:32:08,009 --> 00:32:10,220
Nothing. You're right.

489
00:32:28,363 --> 00:32:30,114
[Chin-nan] Throw me a wiper.

490
00:32:30,115 --> 00:32:31,908
- [Yu-li] Here you go.
- [Yi-hsuan] The competition
is over.

491
00:32:32,033 --> 00:32:36,245
Maybe you should think
about something else.

492
00:32:36,246 --> 00:32:38,414
[Lu-yung] I want more people
to love Taiwanese cuisine.

493
00:32:38,415 --> 00:32:40,292
That's boring.

494
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,086
What about you?

495
00:32:44,254 --> 00:32:45,380
Me?

496
00:32:46,715 --> 00:32:50,260
<i>Confess to me now,
you idiot!</i>

497
00:32:50,385 --> 00:32:52,679
[soft music playing]

498
00:33:04,274 --> 00:33:05,358
What is it?

499
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:08,445
Nothing.

500
00:33:09,446 --> 00:33:12,656
I'm thinking now that
our food truck is so popular,

501
00:33:12,657 --> 00:33:15,410
maybe we should expand
into a fleet

502
00:33:16,203 --> 00:33:18,121
to get more people
to love Taiwanese cuisine.

503
00:33:19,122 --> 00:33:20,457
Yeah.

504
00:33:21,750 --> 00:33:24,044
I think the food truck
is temporary.

505
00:33:25,045 --> 00:33:28,131
We should own
a restaurant after all,
so we need a storefront.

506
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:32,218
But Chang Ta-chin told people
that he'd buy every storefront
you try to rent.

507
00:33:32,219 --> 00:33:34,221
Perhaps you should get real.

508
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:39,142
Maybe it's time.

509
00:33:42,145 --> 00:33:43,480
I'll take you to meet someone.

510
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:46,482
[water splashes]

511
00:33:46,483 --> 00:33:48,692
[squeals]

512
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:51,404
[Yi-hsuan growling]

513
00:33:54,282 --> 00:33:55,784
So cute!

514
00:33:59,329 --> 00:34:00,413
[Shu-min] Hi, Lu-yung.

515
00:34:01,456 --> 00:34:02,999
Hi, Miss Chiang.

516
00:34:03,124 --> 00:34:05,501
Sorry I didn't tell you first.

517
00:34:05,502 --> 00:34:07,337
I wanted
to introduce her to you.

518
00:34:08,296 --> 00:34:11,382
Hi, I'm the manager
of Jin Lai Hao, Chao Yi-hsuan.

519
00:34:11,383 --> 00:34:12,676
I've heard so much about you.

520
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:16,346
I've heard of you
and checked out
your social media.

521
00:34:17,305 --> 00:34:18,390
Thank you.

522
00:34:19,224 --> 00:34:20,725
You're popular now.

523
00:34:20,850 --> 00:34:24,354
I think it's a good idea
to expand
your food truck business.

524
00:34:25,522 --> 00:34:28,692
Yes, it is.
But our boss thinks otherwise.

525
00:34:31,403 --> 00:34:33,363
[chuckles] Tell me.

526
00:34:34,656 --> 00:34:35,740
What is it?

527
00:34:38,368 --> 00:34:40,203
I want to buy a storefront.

528
00:34:40,328 --> 00:34:42,538
I'll mortgage
my old house for a loan

529
00:34:42,539 --> 00:34:44,498
and sell some
of my Chang Xin shares.

530
00:34:44,499 --> 00:34:48,336
That means
your shares will go down,
which changes our original plan.

531
00:34:49,170 --> 00:34:51,297
We've tried many times
to rent a shop,

532
00:34:51,298 --> 00:34:53,550
but we failed again and again.

533
00:34:53,675 --> 00:34:56,552
I know Chairman Chang
has been giving you a hard time,

534
00:34:56,553 --> 00:34:58,429
but I think
you're doing great now.

535
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:00,140
Why do you have
to open a restaurant?

536
00:35:02,100 --> 00:35:04,060
It's what I originally
wanted to do.

537
00:35:04,185 --> 00:35:06,187
A restaurant needs customers
sitting inside
to give it warmth.

538
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:08,732
With our popularity right now,

539
00:35:09,566 --> 00:35:11,568
I think we could plan
for two restaurants
at the same time.

540
00:35:14,738 --> 00:35:17,781
I believe it hit you pretty hard
when Chang Chien-yuan
beat someone up,

541
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:20,243
causing the stock price
to plummet.

542
00:35:21,703 --> 00:35:23,330
You uploaded the video, right?

543
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:27,333
On paper,
I certainly felt the hit.

544
00:35:27,334 --> 00:35:29,460
My boss is professional.

545
00:35:29,461 --> 00:35:31,880
And I know
what young people love.

546
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:35,300
Working together, we absolutely
complement each other.

547
00:35:35,425 --> 00:35:38,261
We can definitely
take Jin Lai Hao further.

548
00:35:44,768 --> 00:35:46,186
Here's the deal.

549
00:35:48,188 --> 00:35:49,563
Don't sell any shares.

550
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:52,442
You won't be able
to buy back your original share.

551
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:54,152
What does that mean?

552
00:35:54,277 --> 00:35:55,904
Just keep to our plan.

553
00:35:56,154 --> 00:35:58,864
I'll help you
with the down payment.

554
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:02,826
[soft upbeat music playing]

555
00:36:02,827 --> 00:36:05,872
We met just now. You don't have
to be so affectionate.

556
00:36:06,706 --> 00:36:07,832
Thank you, Miss Chiang.

557
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:09,501
You'll need to pay me back
at some point.

558
00:36:09,626 --> 00:36:11,877
Right now,
I only want to help you.

559
00:36:11,878 --> 00:36:13,171
I will, I will.

560
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:15,757
I told you it's okay.

561
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:20,178
[singer singing
in foreign language]

562
00:36:25,684 --> 00:36:26,768
[Yi-hsuan] Yes!

563
00:36:28,228 --> 00:36:29,479
[sighs]

564
00:36:30,313 --> 00:36:31,523
Aren't you happy?

565
00:36:32,357 --> 00:36:33,733
Why are you so calm?

566
00:36:34,818 --> 00:36:35,944
Yes!

567
00:36:50,959 --> 00:36:54,963
[singer] <i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

568
00:36:59,676 --> 00:37:03,221
<i>♪ Feeling so strong ♪</i>

569
00:37:03,346 --> 00:37:05,348
<i>♪ Whoa ♪</i>

570
00:37:08,476 --> 00:37:09,978
JIN LAI HAO

571
00:37:11,688 --> 00:37:15,567
<i>♪ Whoa, whoa ♪</i>

572
00:37:16,818 --> 00:37:20,738
<i>♪ Someday, you can
Soar high, fly high ♪</i>

573
00:37:20,739 --> 00:37:24,867
[singing in Mandarin]

574
00:37:24,868 --> 00:37:26,910
[Lu-yung] Watch out!

575
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:29,372
[singer] <i>♪ Somewhere, you can
Find sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

576
00:37:29,497 --> 00:37:33,917
[singing in Mandarin]

577
00:37:33,918 --> 00:37:36,004
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

578
00:37:36,254 --> 00:37:38,256
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

579
00:37:38,381 --> 00:37:40,383
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

580
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:42,385
[singing in Mandarin]

581
00:37:42,510 --> 00:37:46,431
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

582
00:37:46,556 --> 00:37:48,975
[singing in Mandarin]

583
00:37:51,978 --> 00:37:54,481
[Yi-hsuan] Big news! Big news!

584
00:38:02,739 --> 00:38:06,450
Someone anonymously
provided an audio file
to expose a confession

585
00:38:06,451 --> 00:38:09,369
from the heir
of Chang Xin Group,

586
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:13,749
Chang Chien-yuan,
in which he confessed
in a dismissive tone

587
00:38:13,750 --> 00:38:16,294
<i>that in his last year
of high school,
he tailgated a car,</i>

588
00:38:16,419 --> 00:38:18,754
<i>causing it to overturn
and fall over the riverbank,</i>

589
00:38:18,755 --> 00:38:21,381
<i>which killed the driver.</i>

590
00:38:21,382 --> 00:38:24,761
<i>After he hit and ran,
he got his family's driver
to be his scapegoat.</i>

591
00:38:24,886 --> 00:38:26,930
<i>According to our information,</i>

592
00:38:27,055 --> 00:38:29,848
<i>the driver killed
in the crash turned
out to be Chou Chin-lai,</i>

593
00:38:29,849 --> 00:38:32,310
<i>the father of the famous chef,
Chou Lu-yung.</i>

594
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:35,814
<i>As of now, prosecutors
haven't made any statements.</i>

595
00:38:38,525 --> 00:38:40,776
I don't get it. What's going on?

596
00:38:40,777 --> 00:38:42,612
Who spilled the beans?

597
00:38:42,737 --> 00:38:44,531
It doesn't matter at all.

598
00:38:46,533 --> 00:38:49,661
But what's happening
gives us an opportunity.

599
00:38:52,622 --> 00:38:54,957
[Chien-yuan] <i>Back then,
I drove to go after him.</i>

600
00:38:54,958 --> 00:38:56,334
[man] <i>And then?</i>

601
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:58,002
[Chien-yuan] <i>He just skidded.</i>

602
00:38:58,127 --> 00:39:00,964
<i>I was right up on his tail,
and he hit the guardrail.</i>

603
00:39:01,089 --> 00:39:03,715
<i>He flew over and crashed
down the riverbank.</i>

604
00:39:03,716 --> 00:39:05,008
[man] <i>Really?</i>

605
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:06,970
[Chien-yuan]
<i>And Chou Chin-lai...</i>

606
00:39:07,095 --> 00:39:08,096
[man] <i>What?</i>

607
00:39:08,346 --> 00:39:09,556
[Chien-yuan] <i>He died!</i>

608
00:39:10,014 --> 00:39:12,683
<i>When the police saw me,
they were terrified.</i>

609
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:13,934
<i>Who am I?</i>

610
00:39:13,935 --> 00:39:16,813
<i>The heir of Chang Xin!</i>

611
00:39:16,938 --> 00:39:21,109
<i>Some people
are born to be noble,
while some are born to be...</i>

612
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:24,404
[suspenseful music playing]

613
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:40,044
[credits music playing]

614
00:39:46,593 --> 00:39:49,637
[singer singing
in foreign language]

615
00:42:37,263 --> 00:42:38,556
[music ends]
